{{- /*
Resolve whether this machine may install system packages with sudo.

"is_root" is the historical name for "we are allowed to run sudo here". Work
machines default to false because they are often locked down, but plenty of them
do grant sudo, so the answer has to be overridable per machine and it has to
stick.

Single source of truth, included by .chezmoi.toml.tmpl and by every script that
installs system packages. Scripts resolve it here rather than reading .is_root
from the config because chezmoi only re-renders the config template on `init`:
without this, DOTFILES_IS_ROOT=true would be ignored by a plain `chezmoi apply`.

Resolution order:
  1. DOTFILES_IS_ROOT environment override
  2. is_root persisted in chezmoi.toml by a previous init
  3. false on work machines, true otherwise

Returns the string "true" or "false".

Usage: {{ if eq (includeTemplate "is-root" . | trim) "true" }}
*/ -}}
{{- $override := env "DOTFILES_IS_ROOT" -}}
{{- if eq $override "true" -}}
{{-   "true" -}}
{{- else if eq $override "false" -}}
{{-   "false" -}}
{{- else if $override -}}
{{-   fail (printf "DOTFILES_IS_ROOT must be \"true\" or \"false\", got %q" $override) -}}
{{- else if hasKey . "is_root" -}}
{{-   if .is_root }}true{{ else }}false{{ end -}}
{{- else if get . "is_work" | default false -}}
{{-   "false" -}}
{{- else -}}
{{-   "true" -}}
{{- end -}}
